[{:db/id "q-118556/selection/e3a8e2e9b86aa5dbfd708e29d55663cbe169a6d0cba6e3b36e110b885b1235e6" :answer/id #uuid "213504b5-37c4-5932-992d-059063811f2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "570" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118556/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" :answer/id #uuid "e00b73ba-6d3f-5dbc-88a7-d1c4c0694d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118556/selection/311b8a95605ce949d709568e718c3a3acb7e882a6e7faf7eec5a68bead8a815d" :answer/id #uuid "9f16fa97-0187-5da6-ac08-b99d85756335" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "430" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118556/selection/2ae91f4acef1e258303c5198524ee0c09d54456f734e655864530e0fc07a0a9d" :answer/id #uuid "ce18df0d-d2e8-5300-a802-abf911acc97e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "700" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118556/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" :answer/id #uuid "a8d611c0-3f26-5ec6-abe8-af0f27483556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118556/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c3a0e6e-e35f-584a-80a0-05c57473c470" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118556/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" :answer-field/choices ["q-118556/selection/e3a8e2e9b86aa5dbfd708e29d55663cbe169a6d0cba6e3b36e110b885b1235e6" "q-118556/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" "q-118556/selection/311b8a95605ce949d709568e718c3a3acb7e882a6e7faf7eec5a68bead8a815d" "q-118556/selection/2ae91f4acef1e258303c5198524ee0c09d54456f734e655864530e0fc07a0a9d" "q-118556/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118556" :question/id #uuid "bfb7dca1-926a-572e-ba91-5ebc76856166" :question/math-academy-id "q-118556" :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of chimpanzees in a Brazilian forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(1-\\frac{y}{500}),\\,y(0)=70,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible chimpanzee population?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(1-\\frac{y}{500}) \\\\  & =y(\\frac{500-y}{500}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{500}(500-y) \\\\  & =0.002y(500-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=500.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $500,$ and we conclude that the number of chimpanzees cannot exceed $500.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118556/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" :answer/id #uuid "0420c97e-ae1b-595d-b495-dac2d9e272f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854/selection/9ff8157b20b64a245202d0cf913e4397546006c7c38b2b70bb634b860aa35720" :answer/id #uuid "88341dbc-d74e-5b63-a558-cc2a4d3a6d80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer/id #uuid "05cf5567-b599-50e9-b19c-cd2b7dcf818a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "6de42081-df5f-5d3c-a177-9ae2c54fabeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854/selection/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" :answer/id #uuid "23a1df88-27cd-52fe-a4dd-b9b72c2395a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "68614526-0b46-510e-a051-625b2bf9a76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119854/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer-field/choices ["q-119854/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" "q-119854/selection/9ff8157b20b64a245202d0cf913e4397546006c7c38b2b70bb634b860aa35720" "q-119854/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" "q-119854/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" "q-119854/selection/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119854" :question/id #uuid "6a431b28-61ce-5f6e-a7e6-4c7a67f4a70c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119854" :question/problem "The rate of growth in the number of plants $P(t)$ infected with a pest in a certain land follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.5P-0.0025{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=5.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. For which value of $P$ is the number of plants infected with the pest growing at the fastest possible rate?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.5P-0.0025{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0025P(200-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=200.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $200,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 200=100.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119854/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119854"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348209/field-1/4977fa96074bb9b51b40fb6084881ab3f6f490e9ea7ed8e068a1a1cd69dce96b" :answer/id #uuid "61c14c3f-60b2-571c-983b-ddb19aaf6407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348209/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "af0656fa-236e-531d-8ca9-0b6844716ae9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348209/field-1/4977fa96074bb9b51b40fb6084881ab3f6f490e9ea7ed8e068a1a1cd69dce96b" :answer-field/choices ["q-348209/field-1/4977fa96074bb9b51b40fb6084881ab3f6f490e9ea7ed8e068a1a1cd69dce96b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348209" :question/id #uuid "0e36f75d-9145-51ed-9378-85f577b17c08" :question/math-academy-id "q-348209" :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of giraffes on a certain African wildlife reserve follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=14.4y-0.003{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=150,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible population of giraffes?\n\nThe maximum possible population of giraffes is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/d8133f1c4203903bac606bbae61c73717e2ba2dc15a97a77f48eaaeaf4736d06.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =14.4y-0.003{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.003y(4800-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=4800.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $4800,$ and we conclude that the maximum possible population of giraffes is $4800.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348209/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353483/field-1/322d66d6c7db70db7c15f8ad1b0dffa1f638c16211e03217121bc09ed208e6a3" :answer/id #uuid "e5650d47-4d89-573e-b606-9b3c79887688" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353483/field-1/cfb51154c251c8619794ac61783a6985dd38abe0c6e8641008f04453d504a9db" :answer/id #uuid "36e3e12a-97af-5ac0-9fda-ef2bf5a6a9cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353483/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "12e41285-b22e-5a98-bd15-9b5059c5221b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353483/field-1/322d66d6c7db70db7c15f8ad1b0dffa1f638c16211e03217121bc09ed208e6a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-353483/field-1/322d66d6c7db70db7c15f8ad1b0dffa1f638c16211e03217121bc09ed208e6a3" "q-353483/field-1/cfb51154c251c8619794ac61783a6985dd38abe0c6e8641008f04453d504a9db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353483" :question/id #uuid "b846e63d-60e9-5cc7-b977-6cb1960e42bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-353483" :question/problem "The download count $P(t)$ of a viral mobile game follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=4P(8\\,000-P),\\,P(0)=600.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the download count growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=8000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $8000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8000=4000.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353483/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353483"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353490/field-1/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" :answer/id #uuid "0dd73f20-f2ee-5edc-8d9e-7b610627eb27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "450" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353490/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06562415-2d65-5fb0-a1d1-84672c832536" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353490/field-1/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" :answer-field/choices ["q-353490/field-1/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353490" :question/id #uuid "c7b7a1b4-7de9-54a7-9f4b-1f06a4d3bf67" :question/math-academy-id "q-353490" :question/problem "The number $P(t)$ of stores in a retail chain follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=6300P-7{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=50,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the number of stores growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =6300P-7{P}^{2} \\\\  & =7P(900-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=900.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $900,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 900=450.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353490/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
